  "_comment_codeless": "Domains that are code-less BY DESIGN (markdown / SQL / SKILL.md-only) — they have no JS symbols, so they will never appear in the code-symbol architecture map. The Purpose-tab hygiene treats a mapped-but-no-arch domain in this list as INFORMATIONAL (a neutral note), not an actionable 'stale rule' warning. Only add a domain here once you've confirmed it genuinely has no indexable code (vs a dead/mis-targeted rule that should be fixed instead).",
  "codelessDomains": [
    "skills-content",
    "supabase",
    "docs"
  ],
  "_comment_allowedDeps": "BASELINE, NOT ENDORSEMENT (domain-map-reconciliation Phase C, 2026-07-17). Set to the OBSERVED graph AFTER Phase A fixed rule coverage (13 orphaned lib subsystems) and the file-lock move removed the false trapped-primitive edges — so these are real edges, not measurement artifacts. This makes the violation check a RATCHET: it cannot fail on what exists today, only on NEW undeclared edges. THREE entries are recorded debt, NOT intent: (1) shared-lib -> audit-orchestration/claude-hooks/model-eval/nav-audit/stores — ~6 top-level lib files (efficacy-lints, config, repo-inventory, audit-shadow, finalize-outcomes, audit-arms) are feature coordinators, not domain-neutral primitives; retag or move them. (2) stores -> model-eval/persona-test — a LAYER INVERSION: the persistence layer reaching UP into feature domains. (3) cross-skill-bridge -> 11 domains — AGENTS.md calls this a thin facade; eleven deps is not thin. Do not grow these three without fixing the underlying coupling."
